  "title": "CSS Text Spacing",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "CSS Text Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Text Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "CSS has several properties to control text spacing."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "In this chapter you will learn about the following properties:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["text-indent", "letter-spacing", "line-height", "word-spacing", "white-space"]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Text Indentation"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS text-indent property is used to specify the indentation of the first line\nin a text-block."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: Negative values are allowed. The first line will be\nindented to the left if the value is negative."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "p {\n  text-indent: 50px;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_text-indent"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Letter Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS\nletter-spacing property is used to specify the space between the characters in a text."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: Negative values are allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "h1 {\n  letter-spacing: 5px;\n}\n\nh2 {\n  letter-spacing: -2px;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_letter-spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Line Height"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS line-height property is used to specify the space between lines."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Note: Negative values are not allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "p.small {\n  line-height: 0.8;\n}\n\np.big {\n\nline-height: 1.8;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_line-height"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS Word Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS word-spacing property is used to specify the space between\nthe words in a text."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Tip: Negative values are allowed."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "p.one {\n  word-spacing: 10px;\n}\n\np.two {\n  word-spacing: -2px;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_text_word-spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "CSS White Space"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The CSS white-space property specifies how white-space inside an element is handled."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This property can have one of the following values:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": ["normal", "nowrap", "pre", "pre-line", "pre-wrap"]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "css",
      "text": "p {\n  white-space: nowrap;\n}",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_text_white-space"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "The CSS Text Spacing Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["Property", "Description"],
      "rows": [
        ["letter-spacing", "Specifies the space between characters in a text"],
        ["line-height", "Specifies the line height"],
        ["text-indent", "Specifies the indentation of the first line in a text-block"],
        ["white-space", "Specifies how to handle white-space inside an element"],
        ["word-spacing", "Specifies the space between words in a text"]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
